# Data licence — read this before reusing anything in derived/

**This repository does not and cannot license the data it derives.**

## What the sources say

```
1x  Skogsstyrelsen  "open data (Geodataportalen); verify terms before redistributing"
1x  CAL FIRE        "California state open data; see https://data.ca.gov/ and CAL FIRE's terms"
```

The Skogsstyrelsen entry carries a **verify terms before redistributing** flag
that this repository set itself and has never resolved. Sweden is an EU member
state, where a compiled dataset can attract the sui generis database right
independently of copyright, so "open data" on a portal does not by itself settle
redistribution.

The CAL FIRE entry points at terms rather than stating them.

**Both remain unresolved.** Neither supports a CC-BY-4.0 grant downstream.

## Why not CC-BY-4.0

This file previously carried the verbatim CC-BY-4.0 text. Applying CC-BY-4.0
asserts that this repository holds rights it can grant onward. It does not.
**The absence of a stated restriction upstream is not a grant of rights** — it
is silence, and silence cannot be relicensed.

What this repository can say is narrower and true: the capture adds a retrieval
timestamp and a parse. Neither creates a new right over the underlying values.

